{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785183822,"nonce":"EBSiyTM5yRcAg+YbtSPu7GLcKg8=","title":"ADR-0062 s1: Snapshot Farm — give the CAS tree shape on the service's own disk","message":"Materialise a Workspace Snapshot into a directory tree on the **workspace service's own disk**, without asking the network for a byte. The warm CAS is already a local directory (`\u003cwarm_dir\u003e/blobs/\u003csha256\u003e`, `\u003cwarm_dir\u003e/trees/\u003csha256\u003e`), so building a tree only has to reference blobs that are already on the same filesystem.\n\nA Farm is immutable, read-only, keyed by snapshot root, and **shared** by every Step inheriting that snapshot — so fan-out costs nothing.\n\n**Not hardlinks.** Measured (ADR-0062 \"Measured facts\"): a hardlink shares its inode, and mode/mtime live on the inode, so restoring a snapshot's metadata onto a hardlinked entry mutates the CAS blob and corrupts the store for every other snapshot sharing that content. Materialise by `reflink` clone where the filesystem supports it (`FICLONE` on XFS-with-reflink/btrfs, `clonefile` on APFS) and by plain local copy where it does not (ext4 — which is the dogfood disk, so the copy rung is the one that runs locally).\n\n\n- [ ] Given a snapshot root and a warm dir, produces a tree whose content AND metadata match what `S3Storage::local(..).materialize()` produces — that is the existing pinned definition of correct (`crates/scarab-storage-s3/tests/fidelity.rs`)\n- [ ] Exec bit, mtimes, empty directories and symlinks (including a symlink to a directory) all survive\n- [ ] Directory mode/mtime applied in a final reverse pass — creating a child bumps the parent's mtime\n- [ ] **The CAS blob's own mode and mtime are unchanged after a Farm is built and its metadata applied.** This is the anti-corruption test and the most important one in the slice\n- [ ] Reports which rung it took (reflink vs copy) in the return value and in a log line; a run must never be able to silently drop a rung\n- [ ] Idempotent rebuild is cheap, and a partial Farm from a crashed build is never mistaken for a complete one\n- [ ] No network and no object-store dependency in the path\n\n\nNone - can start immediately","files":null}]}